        <div class="section-label">Overview</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Living Ethics</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.85;font-weight:300;margin-bottom:1.2rem;">Agni Yoga, also called Living Ethics (Russian: <em>Zhivaya Etika</em>), is a spiritual teaching first transmitted in 1924. Unlike other yogas focused on physical or meditative disciplines, it is lived in daily life — in thought, action, and relationship.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.85;font-weight:300;margin-bottom:1.2rem;">The teaching calls each student to refine the inner fire of consciousness through service, beauty, and striving toward higher ideals. Central to the teaching is the existence of the Hierarchy of Light and the heart as the link between the human and the cosmic.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.85;font-weight:300;">The series comprises fourteen books composed between 1924 and 1938 by Helena Roerich, with guidance from the Masters of Wisdom. All volumes are available freely online through the Agni Yoga Society.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-label">Core Principles</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">The Path</h2>
        {% for item in [["Beauty", "Consciously created in daily life — in art, in action, in thought. Beauty is called the armour of the spirit."], ["The Heart", "Awakened through striving and love. The heart is the most sensitive receiver and transmitter in nature."], ["Service", "Rendered as an act of spiritual will, not duty. Service to the common good is the highest path."], ["Striving", "Toward higher ideals, always. The fire of the spirit is inexhaustible."]] %}
