  <section id="roerich" style="background:var(--dark-section);padding:5rem 3rem;">
    <div style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="section-label on-dark">The Founders</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading on-dark" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">Helena &amp; Nicholas Roerich</h2>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:4rem;">
        <div>
          <p class="about-body">Helena Roerich (1879–1955) was the author and recorder of the Agni Yoga series, transmitted in collaboration with the Masters of the Agni Yoga Hierarchy. Her extensive Letters provide additional guidance on the path of Living Ethics.</p>
          <p class="about-body">Nicholas Roerich (1874–1947) was a Russian artist, explorer, and peace activist whose Himalayan paintings have become iconic symbols of the spiritual path described in the teachings. He founded the Agni Yoga Society in New York in 1920.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="about-body">Together they worked to make the teachings available to the West, presenting a synthesis of ancient Eastern wisdom and modern Western thought. Nicholas was also the originator of the Roerich Pact, an international treaty for the protection of cultural property.</p>
          <p class="about-body">Their lives and the teaching they transmitted remain inseparable — the paintings, the letters, and the books form a unified body of spiritual instruction for those on the path of conscious evolution.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

